    "result_text": "The late charge is in, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec: the main one and scenarios 1\u20133.\n\n**How it works**\n- **New setting:** a \"Late %\" field (`late-pct`) on the settings form. It takes up to two decimals, is stored as e.g. `10.00`, shows `0.00` until set, and is audited as `SETTING_CHANGED \u2026 key=late-pct value=<percent>`.\n- **The charge:** applies to an OPEN claim whose due-by is before the sheet's today. It is the late percent of the claim's figure for each full 30 days overdue, rounded half to even to two decimals, and added on top. The figure is the bound figure if a statement binds the claim, otherwise the live due after the floor.\n- **Statements:** a statement binds only the figure, not the charge, so the charge keeps moving with the sheet's today.\n- **Settling:** the charge as it stands at that moment is frozen into the settled due. That frozen value is what the clerk-limit check and the `CLAIM_SETTLED \u2026 due=` audit field see.\n- **Totals:** the rollup, the `ROLLUP`/`TOTALS` audit lines, the overdue-total and period due-totals all include the charge. Changing the late percent, the terms or the today therefore writes rollup lines when figures move.\n\n**Two calls the request didn't settle**\n- **Statement due-total:** one of the tests showed that a statement's due-total (the stated total) has to include the charge, even though the figures it binds don't. I changed `TakeStatement` to do that.\n- **Periods:** I also added the charge to period due-totals, on both the server (which fixes the figure when a period is closed) and the screen. The request doesn't say whether periods should include it and no test checks it, so tell me if you'd rather periods leave it out.\n\nThe charge is worked out once on the server in `setting/LatePct.java`, and that is used by the rollup, settling and statements. On the screen it is the `lateCharge` function in `features/claims/Claims.tsx`, used for each claim's due, the people totals and periods.",
